Services are enabled from profile.yaml (`live-session.services`), not by
symlinks here.

There used to be an `etc/dinit.d/boot.d/` with absolute symlinks
(`seatd -> /etc/dinit.d/seatd`). Absolute symlinks in an overlay resolve
against the BUILD HOST, not the image: on a host without seatd installed the
link dangles, artools' overlay copy dereferences it and the build dies with
"cannot stat". It only showed up when the root filesystem was genuinely rebuilt
— every other build reused the cached one and never touched the overlay.

Both services it linked (seatd, NetworkManager) are already in profile.yaml's
service list, so the links were doing nothing except waiting to break.
